-- title:
--   Supersingular DVR with smooth-point packages at q=3
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ denotes `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`, $F :=$ `fieldBar q M'` is the $\bar{\mathbb Q}$-subfield of $\bar{\mathbb Q}((t))$ obtained by base change from the function field of $X_H(q^2M')$ with $H =$ `levelH q M'` the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q)^\times$ (the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$), and $\kappa :=$ `ResidueField A`.
--
--   **Level and base data.** A prime $q$ with $q = 3$; a nonzero $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$; a prime $\ell_0$ with $\ell_0 \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell_0 \mid M'$ (the rigid auxiliary level).
--
--   **Valuation ring and supersingular places.** A valuation subring $A$ of $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ with `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$; a finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` over $\kappa$ (the $\kappa$-field generated inside $\kappa((t))$ by the $q$-expansions `jqModC κ` and `jqNModC κ M'`) such that, by `hW`, $W$ consists exactly of the members of `ssPlaces q M' κ`, namely those places $w$ that are rational (i.e. $\kappa \to w.\mathrm{ResidueField}$ is surjective), satisfy the predicate `IsAffineGeomPlace` and have $w.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of `jGeomGen κ M'` in `ssJSet q κ`; and a chosen $s \in W$.
--
--   **Function fields and the constant reduction.** The hypothesis `hle` that `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, the base change to $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ of the field `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` generated over $\mathbb Q$ by the $q$-expansions $q_d$-expanded from $j$ for $d \mid M'$, is contained in $F$; a structure $R_0 :$ `ConstantReduction A (modularFunctionFieldBar M') (modularFunctionFieldC κ M')`, that is: a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` together with a surjective residue homomorphism onto `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` whose kernel is the maximal ideal, inducing $A \to \kappa$ on constants, such that every nonzero element becomes integral with nonzero residue after multiplication by a suitable constant, plus a map on places preserving degrees and carrying the divisor of a function with nonzero residue to the divisor of its residue; and `hR₀`, requiring that for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\bar{\mathbb Q}((t))$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that image lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R_0$-residue is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ modulo the maximal ideal of $A$.
--
--   **The field of small constants.** An intermediate field $k_0$ of $\bar{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0$ lying in $A$, such that $A \cap k_0$ (formally `A.comap` along $k_0 \to \bar{\mathbb Q}$) is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`) with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ (`hunif`), is henselian (`hhens`) and has algebraically closed residue field (`hres`); and `hκ`, requiring that every $a \in A$ be congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to some $c \in k_0 \cap A$.
--
--   **Auxiliary prime and tame element.** A prime $\ell$ with $\ell \ge 3$, $\ell \ne q$, $\ell \nmid M'$; an element $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ whose image in $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity; an element $\varpi_t \in k_0$ lying in $A$ with $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$.
--
--   **The tower of layers.** An index type $\iota$, a family $K : \iota \to$ intermediate fields of $\bar{\mathbb Q}/k_0$ with each $K_n$ finite over $k_0$, and valuation subrings $A_n$ of $K_n$ with $x \in A_n \iff x \in A$ for all $x \in K_n$.
--
--   Under these hypotheses, with $F$ regarded as a $k_0$-algebra through $k_0 \subseteq \bar{\mathbb Q} \to F$, there exist an intermediate field $F_0$ of $F/k_0$ and a valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$ satisfying the following nine conjuncts.
--
--   (1) *Generation:* the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ in $F$ is all of $F$.
--
--   (2) *Constants:* for $x \in k_0$, $x \in A$ if and only if the image of $x$ in $F_0$ lies in $W_0$.
--
--   (3) $W_0$ is a discrete valuation ring.
--
--   (4) *Uniformiser:* the image of $\pi_0$ in $F_0$ lies in $W_0$ and generates the maximal ideal of $W_0$.
--
--   (5) *Residual transcendence:* there is $t \in W_0$ such that for every polynomial $p$ over $k_0$ all of whose coefficients lie in $A$, if $p(t)$ lies in $W_0$ and in its maximal ideal, then for every $n$ the image in $F_0$ of the $n$-th coefficient of $p$ lies in $W_0$ and in its maximal ideal.
--
--   (6) *Centre at $s$:* for every Laurent series $g$ over $\mathbb Q$ lying in `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose coefficientwise image $\tilde g \in$ `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, assuming that $P.\mathrm{ord}(\tilde g) \ge 0$ for every place $P$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ with $P.\mathrm{ord}$ of the image of `jq` non-negative, and that the $R_0$-residue of $\tilde g$ lies in the valuation subring of the place $s$: the image of $\tilde g$ in $F$ under the inclusion given by `hle` lies in $F_0$, the resulting element of $F_0$ lies in $W_0$, and for every $c \in k_0$ lying in $A$ whose residue in $\kappa$ equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the $R_0$-residue of $\tilde g$, the difference in $F_0$ between that element and the image of $c$ lies in $W_0$ and in the maximal ideal of $W_0$.
--
--   (7) *Level stability:* for every $\zeta$ in `Idx q` (the primitive $q$-th roots of unity in $\bar{\mathbb Q}$) and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M') \subseteq \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$, the automorphism `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` of $F$ over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ — the automorphism characterised by its effect on $q$-expansions of modular forms of level $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$ under embeddings sending $\zeta$ to $e^{2\pi i/q}$, and the identity if no such automorphism exists — maps $F_0$ into $F_0$, and for $f \in F_0$ one has $f \in W_0$ if and only if its image lies in $W_0$.
--
--   (8)–(9) *Prolongations, Drinfeld identification and smooth-point packages:* for every field $F_{ss}$ with a $\kappa$-algebra structure and every $R :$ `RegularProlongation A F F_{ss}` — a valuation subring $R.\mathrm{integers}$ of $F$ with a surjective residue map to $F_{ss}$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal, inducing $A \to \kappa$ on constants, and such that every nonzero element of $F$ becomes integral with nonzero residue after multiplication by a constant — such that for all $f \in F_0$ one has $f \in R.\mathrm{integers}$ if and only if $f \in W_0$, both of the following hold.
--
--   (8) For every $\mathbb F_{q^2}$-algebra structure on $\kappa$, every hypothesis that [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) is a domain and every $\zeta$ in `Idx q`, there are a subgroup $C_s$ of the group of $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of $\mathbb F_{q^2}$ and a $\kappa$-algebra isomorphism $e$ from $F_{ss}$ onto [`DrinfeldCurve.quotField q κ C_s`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelSemistableCoveringW2.html#L32), the fixed field in the Drinfeld function field $\mathrm{Frac}(\mathrm{CoordRing}\,q\,\kappa)$ of the subgroup generated by the actions of the elements $(1,\zeta')$ with $\zeta' \in C_s$, such that $\#C_s = 2\cdot$ `placeWidthChar q M' s`, the latter being `jWidthChar q` of $s.\mathrm{evalAt}(\mathrm{jGeomGen}\,\kappa\,M')$ divided by `placeRamificationJ M' s`; and such that for every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, given that `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹` preserves $R.\mathrm{integers}$ and that $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma, 1)$, the reduction of $\gamma$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb Z/q)$ paired with $1$, lies in [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) (the kernel of the character $(g,u) \mapsto \det(g)\,u^{q+1}$), the automorphism of $F_{ss}$ induced on residues by `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹` is carried by $e$ to the action of that element of `hSubgroup q` on the Drinfeld function field.
--
--   (9) There exist a finite set $N$ of places of $F_{ss}$ over $\kappa$, and for each place $Q$ of $F_{ss}$ over $\kappa$ and each layer $n$ a subring $S_n(Q)$ of $F$, ring homomorphisms $\varphi_n(Q) : A_n[X] \to S_n(Q)$ and $\chi_n(Q) : S_n(Q) \to \kappa$, and a set $D_n(Q)$ of places of $F$ over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$, such that $\#N = q+1$ and the following hold.
--
--   For every $Q \notin N$ and every $n$: the reduction map $A_n \to \kappa$ is surjective; the image of $A_n$ in $F$ lies in $S_n(Q)$; $\varphi_n(Q)$ is formally smooth and formally unramified; $\varphi_n(Q)(C\,a)$ is the image of $a$ in $F$ for $a \in A_n$; $\chi_n(Q)(\varphi_n(Q)(C\,a))$ is the residue of $a$ in $\kappa$; $\chi_n(Q)(\varphi_n(Q)(X)) = 0$; for every $c \in A_n$ with residue $0$ in $\kappa$ there is a unique ring homomorphism $\chi : S_n(Q) \to A_n$ which is the identity on the constants $\varphi_n(Q)(C\,a)$, whose composite with the reduction $A_n \to \kappa$ is $\chi_n(Q)$, and with $\chi(\varphi_n(Q)(X)) = c$; every $f \in S_n(Q)$ lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$, its $R$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $Q$ and reduces in $Q.\mathrm{ResidueField}$ to the image of $\chi_n(Q)(f)$; $\varphi_n(Q)(X)$ lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ and $Q.\mathrm{ord}$ of its $R$-residue is $1$; $D_n(Q)$ consists exactly of the places $P$ of $F$ over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ that are rational, such that every $f \in S_n(Q)$ lies in the valuation subring of $P$ with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f) \in A$, and such that $A.\mathrm{valuation}(P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)) < 1$ if and only if $\chi_n(Q)(f) = 0$; for every ring homomorphism $\chi : S_n(Q) \to A_n$ which is the identity on constants and reduces to $\chi_n(Q)$, there is a unique $P \in D_n(Q)$ with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f) = \chi(f)$ for all $f \in S_n(Q)$; for every $P \in D_n(Q)$ and every $f$ in the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K_n$ in $F$, $f$ lies in the valuation subring of $P$ if and only if $f = g/h$ with $g, h \in S_n(Q)$ and $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(h) \ne 0$; every nonzero $f$ in that compositum with $P.\mathrm{ord}(f) = 0$ for all $P \in D_n(Q)$ satisfies $c \cdot f = u$ in $F$ for some nonzero $c \in K_n$ and some unit $u$ of $S_n(Q)$; every $f$ in that compositum lying in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ and in the valuation subring of every $P \in D_n(Q)$ lies in $S_n(Q)$; and there is a finite subset $G$ of $S_n(Q)$ such that every $f \in S_n(Q)$ satisfies $f\,h = g$ with $g, h$ in the subring generated by $G$ together with the image of $A_n$ and $h$ a unit of $S_n(Q)$.
--
--   For every $Q \notin N$ there is moreover a proof that $K_n \le K_{n'}$ implies $S_n(Q) \le S_{n'}(Q)$, together with: $S_{n'}(Q)$ contained in the subring generated by $S_n(Q)$ and the image of $A_{n'}$ whenever $K_n \le K_{n'}$; the elements $\varphi_n(Q)(X)$ and $\varphi_{n'}(Q)(X)$ having the same image in $F$ for all $n, n'$; and $\chi_{n'}(Q)$ restricting along these inclusions to $\chi_n(Q)$.
--
--   Finally: for $Q, Q' \notin N$, any $n$ and any place $P$ of $F$ over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$, if $P \in D_n(Q)$ and $P \in D_n(Q')$ then $Q = Q'$; for every $Q \notin N$, every $n$ and every $P \in D_n(Q)$, $P.\mathrm{ord}$ of the image of `jq` in $F$ is non-negative; and for every $\tau$ in the subgroup of $\mathrm{Aut}_{\bar{\mathbb Q}}(F)$ generated by the automorphisms `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` with $\zeta$ in `Idx q` and $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, and every hypothesis that $\tau$ preserves $R.\mathrm{integers}$, the automorphism of $F_{ss}$ induced by $\tau$ on residues carries $N$ to itself in the sense that a place $Q$ lies in $N$ if and only if its translate does, and for $Q \notin N$ and every $n$ the translate `smulDisc τ (Dn Q n)` $= \{P : \tau^{-1}\cdot P \in D_n(Q)\}$ equals $D_n$ of the translated place at the same layer.
--
--   This is the $q = 3$ instance of the construction, over an arbitrary admissible field of small constants $k_0$ and an arbitrary family of finite layers $K_n$, of the $k_0$-rational model $(F_0, W_0)$ of the supersingular component of $X_H(q^2M')$ attached to a supersingular place $s$ of $X_0(M')$ in characteristic $q$, together with the identification of the residual field with a quotient of the Drinfeld (Deligne–Lusztig) curve and with étale smooth-point packages — local charts $A_n[X] \to S_n(Q)$, residue characters $\chi_n(Q)$ and residue discs $D_n(Q)$ — at every layer, compatibly with the level automorphisms. It feeds the assembly of the supersingular regular prolongation and its component charts in [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularRegularProlongation_smoothPointCharts_of_eq_three_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularRegularProlongation_smoothPointCharts_of_eq_three_of_dvd), the rigid auxiliary level $\ell_0 \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ being imposed to suppress extra automorphisms of the supersingular points in characteristic $3$.
